id: scavenge
name: Scavenge
prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Survival
requiresSkill: survival
requiresRanks: 2
sessionLimit: 1
timeCost: 2 Hours
# The Check is rolled from the sheet, at the Difficulty the ARC picks there. Ingredients are an Adventure
# Resource not yet in this system: said on the card.
effectNote: makes a Survival Skill Check at a Difficulty Category the ARC decides (rolled from the sheet) - succeeding gains Ingredients: how many and whether any are Special Ingredients depends on how far the Difficulty is exceeded (no more than the number of players in the campaign)
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Two hours foraging in the wilds: a Survival Check at the ARC's Difficulty, and Ingredients if it is
  made - more, and maybe Special ones, the further past it.
text: >
  Scavenge: You search for food in the wilds, coming back with wild vegetables and/or meat.
  –Prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Survival
  –Session Limit: 1
  –Time Cost: 2 Hours
  –Effect: You go out into the wilderness searching for food. Make a Survival Skill Check, with the
  Difficulty Category decided by your ARC (taking into consideration where you begin to Scavenge and
  what is available there). If you succeed, you will gain Ingredients. The amount- and if there’s any
  Special Ingredients- will vary based on how much you exceed the Difficulty Category. The amount of
  Ingredients shouldn’t exceed the number of players in the campaign.

---

# Offered on the Adventure tab to whoever has 2+ Ranks in Survival. Once the two hours are spent the
# card says the Check is owed - rolled from the sheet, where the Difficulty the ARC decides is picked -
# and what it gives. Ingredients are an Adventure Resource, not built yet: how many are gained is the
# ARC's, and keeping them is the table's until they are.
